She's awake!

513
00:32:33,249 --> 00:32:34,624
It's not that bad, is it?

514
00:32:34,832 --> 00:32:37,498
Bad? She's been in a
coma for three years.

515
00:32:38,374 --> 00:32:40,457
You... You are geniuses.

516
00:32:41,291 --> 00:32:42,749
You are magicians.

517
00:32:43,749 --> 00:32:44,790
Many thanks.

518
00:32:45,624 --> 00:32:48,332
Addi, Addi, Addi,
Addi. Addi, tell me.

519
00:32:48,457 --> 00:32:49,498
We need to talk to you.

520
00:32:50,957 --> 00:32:52,748
Who stole the goat?

521
00:32:54,541 --> 00:32:55,541
Munich?

522
00:32:55,707 --> 00:32:56,832
Why Munich?

523
00:32:58,832 --> 00:33:00,498
Wart on the butt.

524
00:33:02,541 --> 00:33:03,999
- Hello?
- Buon giorno.

525
00:33:05,457 --> 00:33:06,498
Come on, Tommie.

526
00:33:09,082 --> 00:33:10,415
Hey, where are you taking him?

527
00:33:10,957 --> 00:33:11,998
There.

528
00:33:13,332 --> 00:33:15,540
You may let go of Henry II now.

529
00:33:17,499 --> 00:33:21,082
Wait a moment. I, I'll
be ready in a second.

530
00:33:23,041 --> 00:33:24,707
There are no dangerous men here.

531
00:33:25,041 --> 00:33:26,624
Move it, potato-head!

532
00:33:29,791 --> 00:33:30,791
Scusi!

533
00:33:33,416 --> 00:33:35,082
Well, how do you feel now?

534
00:33:36,874 --> 00:33:38,207
Suddenly very light.

535
00:33:38,999 --> 00:33:40,165
Everything is lifting off me.

536
00:33:41,249 --> 00:33:44,415
See. The threat only
existed in your head.

537
00:33:47,291 --> 00:33:48,291
Ey, get outta here!

538
00:33:53,541 --> 00:33:55,082
He's alive. Nothing happened.

539
00:34:13,999 --> 00:34:15,040
So, Munich.

540
00:34:15,874 --> 00:34:18,165
And some guy with
a wart on his ass.

541
00:34:18,416 --> 00:34:19,499
Si, we'll get him.

542
00:34:19,999 --> 00:34:23,415
The cup match against the Bayerns isn't
until the day after tomorrow here in Cologne.

543
00:34:23,707 --> 00:34:26,998
If we find the goat in Munich, yeah,
and we bring it here to the stadium...

544
00:34:27,207 --> 00:34:31,373
Ey, they'll freak out. Then we'll
be the super-cops of all Cologne.

545
00:34:31,416 --> 00:34:32,416
Si.

546
00:34:33,457 --> 00:34:35,582
Ey, boah, ey! What a machine!

547
00:34:38,166 --> 00:34:41,749
Tommie, look.
Who's sitting in there.

548
00:34:42,791 --> 00:34:43,791
Ey, that... that's...

549
00:34:45,374 --> 00:34:46,665
That's Jupp.

550
00:34:46,707 --> 00:34:47,748
Wait, wait, wait!

551
00:34:49,416 --> 00:34:50,624
Ey, ey, ey, ey!

552
00:34:50,791 --> 00:34:51,874
Moment!

553
00:34:53,416 --> 00:34:55,332
Good day... Police!

554
00:34:55,999 --> 00:34:57,415
Bicycle squad!

555
00:34:57,999 --> 00:34:59,790
Ey, you still remember me?

556
00:34:59,916 --> 00:35:00,999
From where?

557
00:35:01,041 --> 00:35:03,707
You once gave us
a Cologne-Kalk ban.

558
00:35:03,832 --> 00:35:06,540
Because I was supposed to bring
you a crate of Ramsdorfer Kölsch.

559
00:35:07,207 --> 00:35:08,415
But I didn't do it.

560
00:35:09,291 --> 00:35:12,166
Exactly seven o'clock. With 20
bottles of Ramsdorfer Kölsch.

561
00:35:12,416 --> 00:35:16,499
Just one bottle too few, one
minute too late. Cologne-Kalk ban.

562
00:35:17,207 --> 00:35:18,790
Get out! Now!

563
00:35:20,291 --> 00:35:21,291
Ow!

564
00:35:24,832 --> 00:35:26,082
Driver's license, please.

565
00:35:28,374 --> 00:35:30,915
And the vehicle registration.

566
00:35:31,124 --> 00:35:32,624
And the TÜV. And the ASU.

567
00:35:34,666 --> 00:35:35,666
Please.

568
00:35:38,041 --> 00:35:41,791
Tommie, look.
It's a really ugly picture.

569
00:35:42,207 --> 00:35:46,582
Ey, totally ugly.
Just total crap.

570
00:35:47,041 --> 00:35:48,457
Listen up, my friend.

571
00:35:48,582 --> 00:35:50,665
Don't "please" me. You're
standing right over it.

572
00:35:50,749 --> 00:35:52,957
Let me be. Was that it?

573
00:35:53,457 --> 00:35:54,498
Yes.

574
00:35:54,957 --> 00:35:56,040
Here, please.

575
00:35:57,874 --> 00:35:59,415
Just kidding, just kidding.

576
00:36:00,291 --> 00:36:01,291
Here.

577
00:36:03,999 --> 00:36:05,665
Give me that thing, man.

578
00:36:06,582 --> 00:36:09,582
No, please don't. Please, please!
You're on probation, aren't you.

579
00:36:09,832 --> 00:36:11,540
Oh, oh, oh.

580
00:36:11,832 --> 00:36:14,665
- Jupp, please, please.
- You got pretty lucky there.

581
00:36:14,749 --> 00:36:18,582
Tommie, there's no fine
dust sticker here at all.

582
00:36:20,374 --> 00:36:21,999
Oh, shit!

583
00:36:22,374 --> 00:36:25,290
Sorry, then you can't drive
with this vehicle no more.

584
00:36:26,582 --> 00:36:28,040
Car keys please.

585
00:36:32,499 --> 00:36:34,165
Did you see, Tommie?

586
00:36:34,874 --> 00:36:36,582
Did you see his face?

587
00:36:36,791 --> 00:36:39,999
Boah, man, he was so pissed.
Ey, he's boiling, he's fuming.

588
00:36:40,041 --> 00:36:42,499
Yeah, those shitty cops,
I'm gonna wreck them.

589
00:36:42,541 --> 00:36:45,332
- My beautiful Camaro!
- Yep, yep, yep!

590
00:36:45,499 --> 00:36:49,499
Ey, Mario! Ey, cop, this
is so freaking cool, man.

591
00:36:49,666 --> 00:36:51,999
You can do whatever you want.

592
00:36:52,041 --> 00:36:54,791
And with the Camaro we
are in Munich in no time.

593
00:36:54,791 --> 00:36:56,666
And get Hennes back.

594
00:36:56,707 --> 00:36:57,790
Munich.

595
00:36:57,832 --> 00:37:00,332
What you think, Tommie?
Who kidnapped the goat?

596
00:37:00,624 --> 00:37:01,624
Munich...

597
00:37:02,374 --> 00:37:04,707
Yeah, normal. Ey, Bayern Munich.

598
00:37:05,041 --> 00:37:07,749
Of course, Tommie.
The cup game.

599
00:37:12,749 --> 00:37:16,582
They are scared of the FC, you see.
They want not to lose the cup game.

600
00:37:16,874 --> 00:37:20,082
That Rummenigge there
and Hoeneß and Beckenbauer.

601
00:37:20,124 --> 00:37:23,624
Ey, they're just jealous. 'Cause
they don't have a talisman, see.

602
00:37:24,332 --> 00:37:25,332
Tommie...

603
00:37:25,416 --> 00:37:26,416
Now I know.

604
00:37:26,749 --> 00:37:29,165
On the Sportschau
Hoeneß said it himself:

605
00:37:29,457 --> 00:37:31,457
"With that Franz,
you can steal horses."

606
00:37:31,541 --> 00:37:34,332
- And whoever steals the horses...
- He'll steal a billy goat too!

607
00:37:34,374 --> 00:37:38,165
Madonna. This Beckenbauer I'd
never have thought that of him.

608
00:37:38,166 --> 00:37:40,416
Ey, and someone like
that calls himself Kaiser.

609
00:37:43,666 --> 00:37:45,957
Allora, travel provisions.

610
00:37:46,291 --> 00:37:47,499
And travel beer.

611
00:37:49,499 --> 00:37:51,915
Ey, Mario.
What do we actually do if

612
00:37:51,916 --> 00:37:53,999
Beckenbauer
doesn't want to hand over the goat?

613
00:37:54,041 --> 00:37:57,874
We'll use a police grip. Keep
going until he really snaps.

614
00:37:58,207 --> 00:38:01,790
Normal. But, but what if
the guy gets reinforcements?

615
00:38:02,374 --> 00:38:05,332
Ey, those Bavarians,
they're hard.

616
00:38:05,624 --> 00:38:09,457
Si, Tommie. They'll be stuffing themselves
with such thick white sausages tomorrow.

617
00:38:09,499 --> 00:38:12,249
And at lunch, they'll be shoving
down those pork knuckles.

618
00:38:12,957 --> 00:38:17,457
Ey, those guys, they're big,
ey. And they're totally strong.

619
00:38:22,207 --> 00:38:23,248
Tommie...

620
00:38:23,666 --> 00:38:24,707
we need weapons!

621
00:38:25,082 --> 00:38:26,082
Yeah...

622
00:38:26,374 --> 00:38:27,415
weapons.

623
00:38:33,332 --> 00:38:34,332
And this.

624
00:38:34,374 --> 00:38:35,499
I got a question.

625
00:38:36,124 --> 00:38:38,332
What do you do if
someone mugs you here?

626
00:38:39,832 --> 00:38:40,873
If someone mugs me.

627
00:38:41,332 --> 00:38:42,332
Me.

628
00:38:43,082 --> 00:38:44,582
He'll be crying with joy.

629
00:38:45,374 --> 00:38:49,332
He'll think he's in a nightmare.
Good old Andy prepared for that.

630
00:38:49,999 --> 00:38:54,499
Nice pepper spray in
the eyes, eh. Psh, psh, psh.

631
00:38:54,874 --> 00:38:55,874
Bene, bene.

632
00:38:55,874 --> 00:38:59,165
Yeah, then it's just crying
and spitting and whining.

633
00:39:01,082 --> 00:39:02,957
I love you.

634
00:39:03,916 --> 00:39:07,291
I can do that totally discreetly
with a flick of the wrist.

635
00:39:07,749 --> 00:39:08,749
Elegant.

636
00:39:08,874 --> 00:39:11,665
Shhh! As a surprise, right?

637
00:39:11,749 --> 00:39:13,707
Ey cool. Can I have a look?

638
00:39:16,332 --> 00:39:18,332
I love you.

639
00:39:19,832 --> 00:39:22,665
Or this here. This is
for the real tough ones.

640
00:39:22,707 --> 00:39:25,040
80,000 volts.

641
00:39:26,999 --> 00:39:30,415
Ey, Tommie! This one's
got some real juice in it.

642
00:39:30,457 --> 00:39:33,832
Yeah, for a learning effect, right. The
thief should take something with him too.

643
00:39:34,457 --> 00:39:35,457
Hey!

644
00:39:36,166 --> 00:39:37,166
Ha!

645
00:39:37,874 --> 00:39:38,874
Ho!

646
00:39:42,666 --> 00:39:43,999
Sorry, sorry!

647
00:39:44,041 --> 00:39:45,707
That hit the eye, huh.

648
00:39:46,082 --> 00:39:47,290
Yeah, it's okay.

649
00:39:47,874 --> 00:39:50,124
My lady, it's tingling a bit now, huh.

650
00:40:02,457 --> 00:40:04,790
Alma, stay still.

651
00:40:04,874 --> 00:40:07,040
Oh, man. Now just calm down, hey!

652
00:40:07,041 --> 00:40:10,207
But yeah, there's nothing
you can do now, huh. Just wait.

653
00:40:10,832 --> 00:40:14,415
This here, this isn't some water-soup,
huh. I got this from Moscow, huh.

654
00:40:14,666 --> 00:40:18,207
Old KGB stuff, the good old bromo-acetone.

655
00:40:18,207 --> 00:40:21,332
The eyes are running like a hydrant.

656
00:40:21,999 --> 00:40:23,332
You can see it yourself.

657
00:40:23,999 --> 00:40:25,790
Yeah, it really works well, eh.

658
00:40:26,082 --> 00:40:27,540
Si, perfetto.

659
00:40:29,666 --> 00:40:31,207
Hey, wait, wait, wait.

660
00:40:34,707 --> 00:40:37,373
- Crazy chicken!
- Aspetta, aspetta.

661
00:40:37,791 --> 00:40:38,957
Hey, where is she going?

662
00:40:42,707 --> 00:40:44,457
Oh, shit!

663
00:40:45,124 --> 00:40:46,124
Madonna.

664
00:40:46,291 --> 00:40:47,374
That was the cactus.

665
00:40:48,582 --> 00:40:50,540
But it's also in a bad spot.

666
00:40:55,291 --> 00:40:56,999
Hearty congratulations.

667
00:40:57,832 --> 00:40:59,498
Cool, that girl. Totally.

668
00:41:40,166 --> 00:41:42,916
Ey, Mario. Step on it. We're
practically standing still.

669
00:41:42,957 --> 00:41:44,623
Wait, there's still more in it.

670
00:41:45,957 --> 00:41:49,748
Wow, ey! Cop, this
is so damn cool, ey.

671
00:41:49,791 --> 00:41:51,499
Always full throttle.

672
00:41:55,832 --> 00:41:56,832
Whoops.

673
00:41:57,082 --> 00:41:58,082
Huhu.

674
00:42:05,666 --> 00:42:07,499
Oh, Tommie, let me too.

675
00:42:08,166 --> 00:42:09,166
Sure, sure.

676
00:42:13,749 --> 00:42:14,915
Tommie!

677
00:42:16,082 --> 00:42:17,082
Tommie!

678
00:42:17,832 --> 00:42:18,998
You idiot!

679
00:42:20,374 --> 00:42:22,207
Ey, watch out,
watch out, watch out!

680
00:42:22,291 --> 00:42:23,291
No!

681
00:42:27,041 --> 00:42:29,541
Shit. Shit. Shit. Shit!

682
00:42:44,749 --> 00:42:46,290
Werner, Werner!

683
00:42:46,332 --> 00:42:47,332
What's going on?

684
00:42:49,291 --> 00:42:50,749
Ah, it was you.

685
00:42:50,791 --> 00:42:54,707
Now, now. You gotta go
outside, something came down.

686
00:42:54,749 --> 00:42:56,082
What's supposed to have come down?

687
00:42:56,124 --> 00:42:57,415
That UFO there.

688
00:42:58,166 --> 00:42:59,207
What? A UFO?

689
00:42:59,249 --> 00:43:03,749
Yeah. It was yellow with loads of flames on
it. Please, please, Werner. Go have a look!

690
00:43:04,624 --> 00:43:07,665
Sure, sure, sure.
Women in menopause.

691
00:43:12,999 --> 00:43:15,207
You stupid potato head.

692
00:43:38,249 --> 00:43:41,082
- Buena sera.
- Hello. Police.

693
00:43:41,249 --> 00:43:43,499
Special operation
by the bike squad.

694
00:43:44,624 --> 00:43:45,915
Is this your vehicle?

695
00:43:47,499 --> 00:43:51,249
Good. This is confiscated.
Where are the keys?

696
00:43:54,082 --> 00:43:55,832
Shit, no more gas.

697
00:43:55,874 --> 00:43:58,999
Tommie, we gotta siphon
some from somewhere.

698
00:43:59,457 --> 00:44:00,498
Ah, look there.

699
00:44:01,374 --> 00:44:02,374
That's good.

700
00:44:20,957 --> 00:44:22,040
What is that?

701
00:44:23,207 --> 00:44:24,623
Ey, party.

702
00:44:25,041 --> 00:44:26,166
Ey, awesome.

703
00:44:28,582 --> 00:44:29,582
Va bene.

704
00:44:29,916 --> 00:44:31,707
Tommie, Tommie. Look at you.

705
00:44:31,749 --> 00:44:33,874
You look like a street cop.

706
00:44:43,499 --> 00:44:44,582
Ey, where are you guys from?

707
00:44:44,707 --> 00:44:46,082
Us? From Cologne.

708
00:44:46,416 --> 00:44:47,791
From the bike squad.

709
00:44:48,041 --> 00:44:50,124
Ah, colleagues from
Cologne. Come over here.

710
00:44:52,916 --> 00:44:53,916
Colleague?

711
00:44:53,957 --> 00:44:55,665
Yeah, just open your eyes, eh.

712
00:44:56,707 --> 00:44:57,873
SEK.

713
00:44:58,082 --> 00:45:00,998
Special Deployment Commando.

714
00:45:01,457 --> 00:45:02,457
Wow.

715
00:45:02,624 --> 00:45:04,124
Ey, then a warm welcome, right.

716
00:45:05,999 --> 00:45:08,082
And where exactly in Cologne
are you guys from, huh?

717
00:45:08,291 --> 00:45:09,291
From Kalk.

718
00:45:09,499 --> 00:45:11,499
Ah, don't get me started. Kalk?

719
00:45:11,541 --> 00:45:14,041
Hey, you there.
Wittmann's over there, right?

720
00:45:14,124 --> 00:45:18,540
Yeah, yeah. Exactly. And the other guy here.
What's his name again? Markus Heinrich.

721
00:45:21,791 --> 00:45:25,791
And Markus and I, we two
are like oil and water. Right?

722
00:45:25,791 --> 00:45:27,999
I think I still got
his number here.

723
00:45:27,999 --> 00:45:30,165
- Hold on, I'll call him right now.
- Why, why?

724
00:45:30,207 --> 00:45:31,457
Nah, no need.

725
00:45:31,749 --> 00:45:33,290
Hello. Schorsch here.

726
00:45:33,582 --> 00:45:36,623
Yeah, I got two of your
buddies right here in front of me.

727
00:45:36,749 --> 00:45:39,832
Yeah. You won't believe it,
it's... what are your names again?

728
00:45:40,249 --> 00:45:41,249
Mario.

729
00:45:41,874 --> 00:45:43,082
Ey, Tommie.

730
00:45:43,582 --> 00:45:45,832
Mario and Tommie, right.

731
00:45:46,166 --> 00:45:48,041
Yeah, you're gonna be
floored now, right.

732
00:45:48,832 --> 00:45:49,832
What?

733
00:45:49,999 --> 00:45:53,624
Oh, the father. That's
the father. No offense.

734
00:45:53,624 --> 00:45:55,165
Markus should
give me a call, right.

735
00:46:30,082 --> 00:46:31,123
Markus Heinrich.

736
00:46:31,791 --> 00:46:33,124
Dad, it's a really bad time.

737
00:46:33,582 --> 00:46:34,623
Who called?

738
00:46:34,666 --> 00:46:36,332
Schorsch. Yeah, yeah.
I'll call him back.

739
00:46:37,457 --> 00:46:38,498
Yes, Dad.

740
00:46:39,374 --> 00:46:41,832
No, I can't talk to Mom
right this second.

741
00:46:41,874 --> 00:46:43,040
Then just tell her...

742
00:46:43,041 --> 00:46:44,166
Hello, Mom.

743
00:46:44,166 --> 00:46:45,707
Yeah, I'm doing good.

744
00:46:45,749 --> 00:46:47,249
Mhm, great.

745
00:46:47,291 --> 00:46:49,416
No, I'm taking
care of myself. Yeah.

746
00:46:49,916 --> 00:46:53,791
Same to you guys. Yeah,
I'll call Schorsch. Thanks.

747
00:46:59,707 --> 00:47:02,957
Guys, I gotta introduce
you to two super-girls, right.

748
00:47:07,332 --> 00:47:10,082
This is Petra and
this is Martina.

749
00:47:10,124 --> 00:47:11,540
- Hey, 'sup!
- Hi.

750
00:47:18,832 --> 00:47:20,707
Come on, let's get to it.

751
00:47:25,332 --> 00:47:26,832
He's so cuddly.

752
00:47:30,082 --> 00:47:31,790
Do you guys want to come along?

753
00:47:32,707 --> 00:47:33,707
Where to?

754
00:47:33,749 --> 00:47:35,624
Hey, you'll see then.

755
00:47:36,957 --> 00:47:38,498
Come on, you tiger.

756
00:48:03,791 --> 00:48:05,374
Drop dead, you piece of filth!

757
00:48:18,082 --> 00:48:19,082
Madonna!

758
00:48:19,374 --> 00:48:20,415
Hello?

759
00:48:22,207 --> 00:48:24,748
What happens then, when
it's finished? If I may ask?

760
00:48:24,791 --> 00:48:26,041
They're hitting on our girls.

761
00:48:26,082 --> 00:48:27,623
This is my fiancée. Right?

762
00:48:27,624 --> 00:48:28,790
And this is my wife.

763
00:48:28,832 --> 00:48:31,748
Thilo, please! We
didn't even want to.

764
00:48:32,499 --> 00:48:34,332
They forced us
and threatened us.

765
00:48:34,666 --> 00:48:35,749
What's wrong with those scumbags?

766
00:48:36,082 --> 00:48:37,082
Threatened?

767
00:48:38,291 --> 00:48:40,082
You shove it right
up their asses.

768
00:48:41,291 --> 00:48:43,207
And this is the
thanks for it. Kalle!

769
00:48:44,749 --> 00:48:45,790
